{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>You shall set.</b> Permission:" "<b>Whom YHWH will choose</b> — by a prophet or by the judgment of the Urim. The sense is: not whom you will choose." "<b>You may not.</b> By the way of truth." "<b>Not your brother</b> who is not of the family of Israel, and not an Edomite, even though Scripture calls him \"your brother.\" And because in those days horses were brought out from Egypt — and the proof is the words of Solomon, \"and a chariot came out of Egypt\" — he will need, to multiply his horses, to cause the people to sin by returning to Egypt. And this is clear, for HaShem redeemed them from there, and in their return they profane HaShem. And Uriah the prophet, in danger of his life, fled there; also Jeremiah went there against his will."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:51.636804485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}